Package: gans
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: L-K-M <claudecode@lkmc.ch>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi (>= 3.42), python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-glib-2.0, python3-nacl, python3-xlib, python3-secretstorage, librsvg2-common, gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1 | gir1.2-appindicator3-0.1
Recommends: gnome-keyring | kwalletmanager | keepassxc, polkitd | policykit-1, gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base
Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Homepage: https://github.com/L-K-M/Gans
Description: Ente Auth 2FA codes, one keystroke away (tray agent)
 Gans is a tray-resident client for Ente Auth, the open-source two-factor
 authenticator. It signs in to your Ente account, syncs your codes, and keeps
 them one keystroke away:
 .
  * Quick Search: press the global hotkey (Ctrl+Alt+Space by default), type
    to filter, press Return, and the current code is typed straight into the
    field that had focus before the search appeared.
  * Tray menu: every entry with its live code; click one to copy it.
 .
 Everything is end-to-end encrypted. The account password never leaves the
 machine: it derives the key that unwraps the vault, and is dropped as soon as
 that is done. The session token and the authenticator key are kept in the
 Secret Service (GNOME Keyring, KWallet, or KeePassXC); the on-disk cache holds
 only Ente's already-encrypted entries, so it is useless without the keyring.
 Plaintext secrets exist in memory only, and nothing secret is ever logged.
 .
 No special permission is needed. The hotkey is registered as a GNOME custom
 shortcut, through the GlobalShortcuts portal, or as an X11 key grab, whichever
 the session supports; otherwise bind "gans toggle" yourself. Codes are typed
 through X11 (XWayland under Wayland) and are copied to the clipboard when no X
 server is reachable. The optional app lock asks for your own password through
 polkit before codes are shown.
